IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-sch2`

-- Fraud Act 2006: TESTS FOR SCHEDULE 2 (paragraphs 3 to 11).
--
-- The commencement day used below (1 March 2007) is made up: the Act leaves the real day to an
-- order (section 15(1)).  Each assertion tests one side of it.

§ `Tests for Schedule 2`

§§ `Paragraph 3 and paragraph 11: partly committed`

`the made-up commencement day` MEANS YMD 2007 3 1

-- (a) one relevant event before commencement AND (b) another on or after it.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 4 1) `the made-up commencement day`
-- The later event falls exactly ON the commencement day: "on or after" includes it.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 2 28, YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`
-- Both events before commencement: not partly committed.
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
-- Both on or after commencement: not partly committed.
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 3 1, YMD 2007 4 1) `the made-up commencement day`
-- A single event cannot be both before and on or after.
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 3(2) and 11(2): the offence was partly committed before the commencement` (LIST YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`

§§ `Paragraph 3(1): what becomes of liability for an old deception offence`

-- Partly committed: liability is saved.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1): what becomes of liability for an old deception offence` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 4 1) `the made-up commencement day` EQUALS `liability is saved by paragraph 3 of Schedule 2`
-- Wholly on or after commencement: the offence had been omitted by Schedule 1 paragraph 1, so no liability under it.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1): what becomes of liability for an old deception offence` (LIST YMD 2007 3 1, YMD 2007 4 1) `the made-up commencement day` EQUALS `the offence was abolished before any of its relevant events: no liability under it`
-- Wholly before commencement: Schedule 2 says nothing (it saves only offences partly committed before).
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1): what becomes of liability for an old deception offence` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day` EQUALS `the Act does not say (every relevant event was before commencement, or none is given)`
-- No relevant event given: the Act does not say (the empty case is not read as "abolished").
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 3(1): what becomes of liability for an old deception offence` EMPTY `the made-up commencement day` EQUALS `the Act does not say (every relevant event was before commencement, or none is given)`

§§ `Paragraphs 4 to 10: savings for provisions of other Acts`

-- The shape: circumstances apply AND the deception (or credit) came strictly before commencement.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 4 to 10: the saving applies` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 4 to 10: the saving applies` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 4 to 10: the saving applies` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 2) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraphs 4 to 10: the saving applies` FALSE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`

-- Paragraph 4 (Theft Act 1968 s 24), 5 (s 24A(7), (8)), 6 and 7 (Northern Ireland twins), 8 (Limitation Act 1980 s 4),
-- 9 (Limitation (NI) Order 1989 Art 18), 10 (Terrorism Act 2000 Part 7): each saved on the day before, none on the day.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 4: paragraph 6 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 24 of the Theft Act 1968` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 4: paragraph 6 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 24 of the Theft Act 1968` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 5: paragraph 7 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 24A(7) and (8) of the Theft Act 1968` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 5: paragraph 7 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 24A(7) and (8) of the Theft Act 1968` FALSE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 6: paragraph 11 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 23 of the Theft Act (Northern Ireland) 1969` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 6: paragraph 11 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 23 of the Theft Act (Northern Ireland) 1969` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 2) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 7: paragraph 12 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 23A(7) and (8) of the Theft Act (Northern Ireland) 1969` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 7: paragraph 12 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 23A(7) and (8) of the Theft Act (Northern Ireland) 1969` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 8: paragraph 18 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 4 of the Limitation Act 1980` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 8: paragraph 18 of Schedule 1 does not affect section 4 of the Limitation Act 1980` FALSE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 9: paragraph 22 of Schedule 1 does not affect Article 18 of the Limitation (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 9: paragraph 22 of Schedule 1 does not affect Article 18 of the Limitation (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` TRUE (YMD 2007 3 1) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 10: paragraph 30 of Schedule 1 does not affect Part 7 of the Terrorism Act 2000` TRUE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 10: paragraph 30 of Schedule 1 does not affect Part 7 of the Terrorism Act 2000` FALSE (YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`

§§ `Paragraph 11: powers of arrest`

-- Partly committed before the commencement of paragraph 35 of Schedule 1: the power of arrest is unaffected.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 paragraph 11(1): paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 does not affect the power of arrest conferred by section 14 of the 2004 Act` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 4 1) `the made-up commencement day`
#ASSERT NOT `Schedule 2 paragraph 11(1): paragraph 35 of Schedule 1 does not affect the power of arrest conferred by section 14 of the 2004 Act` (LIST YMD 2007 1 15, YMD 2007 2 28) `the made-up commencement day`
